  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the establishment of a Syrian mine action authority and enhancing national and international mine action capacities to reduce the risk from explosive ordnance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;This project, aligned with the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) 2025, and the UN Strategic Framework (2022&#xbf;2025), aims to establish a sustainable national mine action architecture. Its core objectives are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Establishment of a National Mine Action Authority (NMAA) under a developed legal and policy framework&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Operationalization of a capacitated National Mine Action Center (NMAC)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Safe delivery of aid and services by humanitarian and early recovery actors, and safe access for civilians&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;To achieve these goals, UNMAS will support the Ministry of Emergency and Disaster Management (MoEDM) in developing legal frameworks, national standards, and strategic plans. UNMAS will provide technical assistance in institutional development, coordination, and quality assurance systems. The project will also promote inclusive practices, enhance public awareness, and strengthen information and operations management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Operationally, UNMAS will equip and train national teams, including the necessary oversight and monitoring of these aspects, under the Ministry to enable mine action activities to be conducted to international standards, including survey, clearance, and explosive ordnance risk education. UNMAS will also, through its own partners, carry out Non-Technical Survey (NTS), Technical Survey (TS), Explosive Ordnance Disposal (EOD), and mechanical and manual clearance operations in priority governorates to directly support humanitarian and early recovery projects. As the de facto coordinating authority for mine action in Syria, UNMAS will continue to lead sector-wide engagement, ensuring that operators are accredited, tasks are prioritized, and information is managed transparently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;By building national capacity and delivering targeted interventions, this project lays the foundation for a safer Syria, where recovery is not only possible, but resilient, inclusive, and locally led&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
